{
  "about": "What Go's strconv.ParseFloat(in, 64) returns for each input, as the settings layer's floatField decodes a stored value: a number; \"+Inf\", \"-Inf\" or \"NaN\", which JSON cannot carry; \"-0\", which a JSON reader may re-serialize as 0 (Vite does); or null where ParseFloat returns an error (ErrSyntax or ErrRange) and the stored value is skipped. utils/goParseFloat.ts is tested against this file, and internal/adapters/sqlstore checks it against floatField itself, so neither side can drift from the other.",
